# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the UUSE/TiKV integration (Shard-118).
#
# SPDK/DPDK are prebuilt without instrumentation, so the happens-before edges
# of spdk_thread_send_msg and bdev completions are invisible to TSAN. Only the
# frames that sit directly on that boundary are suppressed; instrumented UUSE
# and shim code must stay clean.
race:uuse::SpdkRuntime::Impl::controlSubmitTrampoline
race:uuse::SpdkRuntime::Impl::submitControlIo
